{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"d549bd4745246ec1e40602e4c8de1a974e64817ff11d5500c333414cba00db0a","digest":{"component_or_area":"completion recovery and close gate","key_entities":["_MAX_CONTEXT_CHARS","_MAX_TOTAL_CRITERIA_CHARS","completion_recovery.py","transition_close.py","CompletionRecoveryError","recovery_failure_cause","assemble_context","test_completion_recovery_oversized_d59e.py","test_close_gate_step_budget_message_d59e.py","docs/llm-framework.md"],"problem_keywords":["completion recovery context bound","step-budget failure messaging","close gate availability defect","bounded recovery cost safeguard","false remedy attribution"],"propositions":["A ticket with large text (34,282 or 41,595 chars) cannot transition to closed state because bounded recovery refuses context over 24,000 chars before performing any work.","When step-budget exhaustion occurs during completion verification, the close gate incorrectly reports 'install the agents extra' instead of the exception's own remedy, because recovery_failure_cause returns None for non-CompletionRecoveryError exceptions.","The criteria budget (32,000 chars) exceeds the context budget (24,000 chars), creating an incoherent state where valid criteria can be rejected on context grounds alone.","Raising the context cap to 100,000 chars and removing elision allows oversized tickets to reach a verdict while maintaining the fail-closed cost safeguard that prevents billable recovery calls on breach."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787412161234595001,"uuid":"6ac4c2e9-4e38-4abd-a01d-3422af2ade76"}